WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.100
Tesla and SpaceX confirmed a $16.8 billion first phase for the TerraFab chip plant that will target

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:14.200
more annual ai compute output than the entire planet currently produces. This is Tesla Shorts Time,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:21.820
Episode 564. The company's plan the largest chip manufacturing facility ever on the Grimes County

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:29.700
site. Output is targeted at over one terawatt of annual ai compute. Both Tesla and SpaceX

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:35.560
need far more chips than current global production can supply. The prototype phase alone

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:43.460
requires an estimated $119 billion in total investment. Full buildout is projected between 5 trillion

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:51.500
and 13 trillion dollars. TerraFab ai compute output is planned at roughly 25% for Tesla Optimus

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:59.680
and 75% for ai spacecraft. The first phase investment is expected to create over 3000 new jobs in

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:05.720
the initial year. The fully built out complex is projected to cover up to 10 million square meters,

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:13.380
roughly 11 times larger than Giga Texas. Yesterday's announcement marks the first concrete step beyond

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:19.740
the research fab already under construction on the north campus of Giga Texas. This scale of new

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:25.240
compute infrastructure connects directly to how that compute will eventually power vehicles on the

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:32.000
road. Tesla Roddy shared interior images of the Tesla CyberCab. The passenger cabin shows no

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.860
steering wheel or pedals. This design confirms the vehicle's intended unsupervised robo taxi focus.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:45.620
The minimalist layout centers on passenger space rather than driver controls. Production timing

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:52.240
and regulatory approval for driverless service remain the main open questions. No production start

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:58.180
date or pricing details appeared in the post. While the CyberCab targets passenger service,

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:05.380
another autonomous concept appeared alongside Optimus. Elon Musk shared footage of the robo van concept

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:12.280
mixed with renderings of the future TerraFab campus. The vehicle features a boxy, windowed body suited

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:18.100
for multiple passengers. The design appears aimed at autonomous mass transit use cases.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:24.900
The clip includes early glimpses of the planned TerraFab complex. Current prototype elements

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:31.720
sit alongside facility renderings in the same video. Shifting from future robo taxis and robo vanes

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:38.400
brings us to current energy storage deployments already scaling. Tesla began MegaPak 3 production

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:45.400
at the new Brookshire Mega Factory in Texas. The facility reached operation just 16 months after

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:52.300
groundbreaking. It holds 50 gigawatt hours of dedicated annual capacity. A separate line handles

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:59.020
the MegaPak 3 variant. This adds substantial utility scale storage at a time when grid operators

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:05.280
are signing large battery contracts. Production start at this scale directly increases available

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:12.380
supply for utility projects. New factory output is already feeding real projects, including one that

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:19.360
just went live. A 500 megawatt hour Tesla MegaPak battery site is now operational in Texas.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:26.220
The installation supports grid stability in a single large deployment. Texas continues to see rapid

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:33.200
additions of utility scale storage as demand for flexible capacity grows. The project adds to the

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:39.040
state's expanding network of Tesla energy systems. No customer name or exact location beyond

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:45.560
Texas was disclosed in the report. While energy hardware scales steadily, supervised autonomy

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:52.800
continues to show both progress and friction. An owner reported a supervised FSD near miss on a

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:59.080
highway entry. The vehicle repeatedly swerved while unable to settle on a single route. The driver

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:04.580
experienced with the system since version 11 called it the first serious safety concern.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:09.060
The vehicle averaged conflicting route options before the driver intervened.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:16.500
No damage or contact occurred in the reported event. Domestic FSD challenges contrast with

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:23.300
Tesla's push for broader regulatory approval. Tesla is seeking EU-wide approval for supervised

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:31.400
full self-driving. The application covers all 27 member states. Dutch data secrecy rules add complexity

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:37.980
for training data access. Approval would open a large new market for the feature. No timeline for a

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:44.180
decision was provided in the filing summary. Regulatory hurdles for software sit alongside hardware

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:50.900
production setbacks that have now eased. Cybertruck production at Giga Texas has resumed after a court

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:58.340
ruling on tooling access. Inventory levels at the factory are rising again. The episode underscores how

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:04.440
single-supplier dependencies can still affect vehicle ramp timelines. The court decision cleared

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:10.660
the path for immediate resumption of body and chassis assembly. No production rate figures were

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:16.600
released in the coverage. Production stability for vehicles pairs with expanding third-party charging

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:25.660
access. EVIO plans to build out 22 new Tesla supercharger locations. Each site will include 325

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:32.680
kilowatt and 500 kilowatt stalls. This expands the open access portion of the network in additional

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:39.340
U.S. markets. Utilization data from these new locations will show how non-Tesla drivers adopt

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:46.500
the chargers. No specific cities or timelines for individual openings were listed. Charging access

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:53.220
supports adoption, which state incentives can further accelerate. California updated its $3,500

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:59.640
EV rebate rules. Several Tesla models qualify under the new income and price criteria.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:07.640
The program targets lower income buyers. The rebate amount remains fixed at $3,500 for qualifying

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:13.400
purchases. Exact model year cutoffs and income thresholds were detailed in the state guidance.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:20.000
Policy support for vehicles contrasts with competitive pressure in robotics. A Chinese robot

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:27.020
maker plans a $9 billion IPO. The valuation focuses on lighter industrial and service rules.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:32.480
Volume manufacturing economics remain the central open question for both efforts.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:38.120
The firm has targeted applications different from Tesla's Optimus program to date.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:45.040
No direct head-to-head performance data was included in the valuation analysis. Competition in

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:51.820
robotics returns us to the massive compute bet that underpins Optimus scale. Details on an older

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:58.740
300 storage megapak site in Texas have emerged. The installation adds to the growing list of utility

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:05.620
scale projects now live. Local deployment pace shows continued momentum for Tesla energy outside

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:12.300
vehicle sales. Connection timelines and expected output contribution were shared. No customer or

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:18.600
utility partner name was released with the facts. Tesla rolled out a new maps update across North

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:24.420
America. The package includes revised street layouts, updated speed limits and refreshed points

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:30.740
of interest. Vehicles receive the changes through over the air delivery. Accurate mapping remains

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:37.640
foundational for both navigation and supervised FSD performance. The update covers the United States,

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:45.100
Canada and Mexico in a single package. Now one thing worth watching is the supervised FSD near miss

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:51.580
reported by an owner on a highway entry. The vehicle repeatedly swerved while deciding whether to

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:58.500
enter the highway, forcing manual intervention to avoid the median. The driver experienced with

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:04.080
version since 11 described this as the first incident that raised serious safety concerns.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:10.600
Resolving inconsistent route choice behavior remains necessary before unsupervised operation can

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:17.260
advance. The post notes the vehicle could not settle on a single path and oscillated between options.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:24.680
No regulatory filing or Tesla response has been issued yet. The decision to locate a multi-trillion

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:31.260
dollar semiconductor campus in Grimes County rests on a simple physical constraint. Orbital solar

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:37.580
delivers roughly five times the energy density of ground-based arrays while space itself provides

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:44.120
free convective cooling. Placing the majority of tariff abs output into low-earth orbit satellites,

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:50.280
therefore sidesteps both land use limits and the massive water infrastructure that terrestrial AI

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:57.060
clusters require. The remaining quarter of capacity reserved for terrestrial edge inference directly

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:03.920
funds the scale of Optimus deployment Tesla has described. This allocation also changes the capital

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:09.640
math because a conventional fab spreads its cost across consumer electronics and automotive chips

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:16.880
with relatively predictable margins. Terrafabs economics instead tie returns to two high uncertainty

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:24.000
bets. The regulatory path for unsupervised autonomy on Earth and the launch cadence of AI satellites.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:30.640
The 3000 jobs projected for the first phase already exceed the staffing of most modern semiconductor

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:37.180
plants, even before Optimus robots handle construction and maintenance at full scale. Before we go,

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:43.120
the next update on the Brookshire Megafactory output figures should clarify how quickly utility

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:50.260
scale contracts can be fulfilled. That covers it for today's Tesla developments. TSLA closed at

